IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain

-- g9-interpretation.l4: the fork points of group G9 (Schedules 1 and 2), one enumeration per fork, one record `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` whose fields are the fork points,
-- and the named interpretations the tests hand to the public decisions.  This file is the artefact; the 20 near-identical named interpretations at the end were written out by a small script from the table of forks (encoder scratch, not shipped), so a change to a fork is a change to every one of them: edit them together.
-- Every public decision of G9 that depends on a fork takes this record as an ordinary GIVEN and delegates by CONSIDER to one private implementation per reading.
-- TYPICALLY records the favoured reading of each fork; in this release it is metadata and the field is still supplied at every construction (the named interpretations below do so).
-- F9.13 is typed with `Unit of a term of imprisonment` from domain.l4, so that the integrator can set F6.16, F7.8, F8.8 and F9.13 from one value (IP35).

§ `Fork points of Schedules 1 and 2`

-- F9.1: readings A to B of `the 2 weeks before an appointment`
DECLARE `How the 2 weeks before an appointment are counted` IS ONE OF
    `the appointment is 14 or more days after the notice`
    `there are 14 clear days between the notice and the appointment`

-- F9.2: readings A to B of `the 6 years of an appointment`
DECLARE `How the 6 years of an appointment are counted` IS ONE OF
    `the end date is the day the term expires`
    `the end date is the last day of the term`

-- F9.3: readings A to C of `a resignation on notice`
DECLARE `How a resignation on notice takes effect` IS ONE OF
    `the office ends when the notice period runs out, the months being clamped`
    `the office ends when the notice is given`
    `the office ends when the notice period runs out, the months being rolled`

-- F9.4: readings A to B of `an absence from duties`
DECLARE `How an absence from duties is counted` IS ONE OF
    `the days of absence are counted, the first and the last included`
    `the elapsed days from the first to the last day of absence are counted`

-- F9.5: readings A to B of `the 2 weeks after a termination`
DECLARE `How the 2 weeks after a termination are counted` IS ONE OF
    `the 14th day after the termination day is in time`
    `the termination day is day 1, so the 13th day after it is the last in time`

-- F9.6: readings A to B of `twelve years of service`
DECLARE `How twelve years of service are counted` IS ONE OF
    `twelve calendar years measured in days from the first day of service`
    `twelve years of 365 days`

-- F9.7: readings A to B of `the 4 months after the end of the year`
DECLARE `How the 4 months after the end of the year are counted` IS ONE OF
    `the months are added and the day is clamped to the end of the month`
    `the months are added and the day is rolled into the next month`

-- F9.8: readings A to B of `the decision under Article 15(3)`
DECLARE `Which outcomes of the decision under Article 15(3) are reserved from staff` IS ONE OF
    `both outcomes of the decision are reserved`
    `only the refusal is reserved`

-- F9.9: readings A to B of `a cost directed to the Fund`
DECLARE `Who bears a cost that an Order under the Dormant Bank Accounts Law directs to the Fund` IS ONE OF
    `the Fund bears the cost in place of the annual income of the States`
    `the States remain liable and the Fund only reimburses`

-- F9.10: readings A to B of `as soon as practicable`
DECLARE `How as soon as practicable is measured` IS ONE OF
    `as soon as practicable is a judgement supplied as an input`
    `as soon as practicable is a number of days from the day the step falls due` HAS `number of days` IS A NUMBER

-- F9.11: readings A to B of `service as a designated relevant person`
DECLARE `Whether service as a designated relevant person counts toward twelve years` IS ONE OF
    `service as a designated relevant person does not count`
    `service as a designated relevant person counts`

-- F9.12: readings A to B of `a year in which the office was held for only part of it`
DECLARE `Whether a report is required for a part-year` IS ONE OF
    `a report is required for the part of the year in which the office was held`
    `a report is required only for a whole calendar year`

-- F9.13: `the unit of the cap on imprisonment` is typed by domain.l4's `Unit of a term of imprisonment` (readings: `calendar months`, `days`).

-- F9.14: readings A to B of `before appointing`
DECLARE `How before appointing is counted for the views that must be sought` IS ONE OF
    `the views were sought on an earlier day than the day of the appointment`
    `the views were sought on or before the day of the appointment`

-- F9.15: readings A to B of `a vacant office of chair or vice-chair`
DECLARE `Whether a vacant office of chair or vice-chair counts as absent` IS ONE OF
    `a vacant office counts as absent`
    `a vacant office is not covered and the Law does not answer`

-- F9.16: readings A to B of `the decision on entry in the restricted section`
DECLARE `Whether the decision on entry in the restricted section is reserved from staff` IS ONE OF
    `it is not reserved because it is not a decision under Article 11`
    `it is reserved as part of the decision whether to register`

-- F9.17: readings A to B of `membership of the States when appointed`
DECLARE `Whether a person who is already a member of the States is caught` IS ONE OF
    `only becoming a member during the appointment ends it`
    `being a member at any time during the appointment ends it`

-- F9.18: readings A to B of `the responsible officer where several members of staff are available`
DECLARE `Who is the responsible officer where more than one member of staff is available` IS ONE OF
    `the one member of staff the Minister has named is the responsible officer`
    `every member of staff available is the responsible officer`

-- F9.19: readings A to B of `the ground of absence for terminating an appointment`
DECLARE `Whether the ground of absence must exist in fact as well as in the Minister's mind` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister's satisfaction and the absence longer than the number of weeks are both required`
    `the Minister's satisfaction alone is required`

-- The record: one field per fork point, each TYPICALLY the favoured reading (reading A of every fork).
DECLARE `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
    HAS `the 2 weeks before an appointment` IS A `How the 2 weeks before an appointment are counted`
            TYPICALLY `the appointment is 14 or more days after the notice`
        `the 6 years of an appointment` IS A `How the 6 years of an appointment are counted`
            TYPICALLY `the end date is the day the term expires`
        `a resignation on notice` IS A `How a resignation on notice takes effect`
            TYPICALLY `the office ends when the notice period runs out, the months being clamped`
        `an absence from duties` IS A `How an absence from duties is counted`
            TYPICALLY `the days of absence are counted, the first and the last included`
        `the 2 weeks after a termination` IS A `How the 2 weeks after a termination are counted`
            TYPICALLY `the 14th day after the termination day is in time`
        `twelve years of service` IS A `How twelve years of service are counted`
            TYPICALLY `twelve calendar years measured in days from the first day of service`
        `the 4 months after the end of the year` IS A `How the 4 months after the end of the year are counted`
            TYPICALLY `the months are added and the day is clamped to the end of the month`
        `the decision under Article 15(3)` IS A `Which outcomes of the decision under Article 15(3) are reserved from staff`
            TYPICALLY `both outcomes of the decision are reserved`
        `a cost directed to the Fund` IS A `Who bears a cost that an Order under the Dormant Bank Accounts Law directs to the Fund`
            TYPICALLY `the Fund bears the cost in place of the annual income of the States`
        `as soon as practicable` IS A `How as soon as practicable is measured`
            TYPICALLY `as soon as practicable is a judgement supplied as an input`
        `service as a designated relevant person` IS A `Whether service as a designated relevant person counts toward twelve years`
            TYPICALLY `service as a designated relevant person does not count`
        `a year in which the office was held for only part of it` IS A `Whether a report is required for a part-year`
            TYPICALLY `a report is required for the part of the year in which the office was held`
        `the unit of the cap on imprisonment` IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment`
            TYPICALLY `calendar months`
        `before appointing` IS A `How before appointing is counted for the views that must be sought`
            TYPICALLY `the views were sought on an earlier day than the day of the appointment`
        `a vacant office of chair or vice-chair` IS A `Whether a vacant office of chair or vice-chair counts as absent`
            TYPICALLY `a vacant office counts as absent`
        `the decision on entry in the restricted section` IS A `Whether the decision on entry in the restricted section is reserved from staff`
            TYPICALLY `it is not reserved because it is not a decision under Article 11`
        `membership of the States when appointed` IS A `Whether a person who is already a member of the States is caught`
            TYPICALLY `only becoming a member during the appointment ends it`
        `the responsible officer where several members of staff are available` IS A `Who is the responsible officer where more than one member of staff is available`
            TYPICALLY `the one member of staff the Minister has named is the responsible officer`
        `the ground of absence for terminating an appointment` IS A `Whether the ground of absence must exist in fact as well as in the Minister's mind`
            TYPICALLY `the Minister's satisfaction and the absence longer than the number of weeks are both required`

§§ `The named interpretations`

-- The favoured interpretation: reading A of every fork.
`the favoured interpretation` MEANS `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2` WITH
        `the 2 weeks before an appointment` IS `the appointment is 14 or more days after the notice`
        `the 6 years of an appointment` IS `the end date is the day the term expires`
        `a resignation on notice` IS `the office ends when the notice period runs out, the months being clamped`
        `an absence from duties` IS `the days of absence are counted, the first and the last included`
        `the 2 weeks after a termination` IS `the 14th day after the termination day is in time`
        `twelve years of service` IS `twelve calendar years measured in days from the first day of service`
        `the 4 months after the end of the year` IS `the months are added and the day is clamped to the end of the month`
        `the decision under Article 15(3)` IS `both outcomes of the decision are reserved`
        `a cost directed to the Fund` IS `the Fund bears the cost in place of the annual income of the States`
        `as soon as practicable` IS `as soon as practicable is a judgement supplied as an input`
        `service as a designated relevant person` IS `service as a designated relevant person does not count`
        `a year in which the office was held for only part of it` IS `a report is required for the part of the year in which the office was held`
        `the unit of the cap on imprisonment` IS `calendar months`
        `before appointing` IS `the views were sought on an earlier day than the day of the appointment`
        `a vacant office of chair or vice-chair` IS `a vacant office counts as absent`
        `the decision on entry in the restricted section` IS `it is not reserved because it is not a decision under Article 11`
        `membership of the States when appointed` IS `only becoming a member during the appointment ends it`
        `the responsible officer where several members of staff are available` IS `the one member of staff the Minister has named is the responsible officer`
        `the ground of absence for terminating an appointment` IS `the Minister's satisfaction and the absence longer than the number of weeks are both required`

